#{[{:activity/expected-seconds 1080.0 :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186125406} :activity/id #uuid "9ba6f288-55b6-582e-8aa1-d15ec442bd9c" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050376 :topic/id #uuid "44312a5e-e7e0-507f-86f6-c3bcdecfd7fe" :topic/math-academy-id 1964} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186125406 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186125785 :tutorial/content "We can find the eigenvalues of a $3\\times 3$ matrix in much the same way as for $2\\!\\times\\! 2$ matrices. \n\nRemember, $\\lambda$ is an eigenvalue of $A$ if $A\\mathbf{v} = \\lambda\\mathbf{v}$ for some non-zero vector $\\mathbf{v}$. This implies that the equation\n\n$$\n(A-\\lambda I)\\mathbf{v}=\\mathbf{0}\n$$\n\nhas a non-trivial solution, which means that the matrix $A-\\lambda I$ is singular, and consequently\n$\\textrm{det}(A-\\lambda I)=0.$\nTherefore, if we want to find the eigenvalues of a $n\\!\\times\\! n$ matrix $A,$ we have to find the solutions of the characteristic equation\n\n$$\n\\textrm{det}(A-\\lambda I)=0.\n$$\n\nLet's go through this process in the case of the matrix $A,$ given by\n\n![](images/21/21e0994519fbba32a84020ce4661e98600c1307947083ddc3afe9902658143c1.svg)\n\nFirst, we write down the matrix $A-\\lambda I{:}$\n\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A-\\lambda I & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -8 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}\\lambda  & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\lambda  & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & \\lambda \\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2-\\lambda  & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -8-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5-\\lambda \\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we set and solve the characteristic equation $\\,\\textrm{det}(A-\\lambda I)=0.$ Using the fact that the determinant of a triangular (or diagonal) matrix is given by the product of the elements on the main diagonal, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}-2-\\lambda  & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -8-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (-2-\\lambda )(-8-\\lambda )(5-\\lambda ) & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda +2)(\\lambda +8)(\\lambda -5) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the eigenvalues of the matrix $A$ are $\\lambda=-2,$ $\\lambda=-8,$ and $\\lambda=5.$" :tutorial/id #uuid "535c5b8b-f815-5ded-8ae5-668bac420af7" :tutorial/math-academy-id 3564 :tutorial/title "Introduction"} :step/id #uuid "9f05d37d-484a-5ae0-8ed9-0b46584f4a7f" :step/math-academy-id 20093 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186125407}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186125407 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124522 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124331 :question/id #uuid "4b2fcf5d-0da3-5676-b4c6-54095c3fb45c" :question/math-academy-id "e-5486"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "289ae874-f555-50ee-896f-eb2188004124" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049159} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050001}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186125012} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186125017} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186323857} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186323904} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186323909} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186400881} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186427385}] :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Eigenvalues of a 3x3 Matrix Containing a Block of Zeros"} :step/id #uuid "9edf1314-60a8-581e-afc3-f39ecd8b7951" :step/math-academy-id 20094 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186125408}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186125408 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186125786 :tutorial/content "The **algebraic multiplicity** of an eigenvalue $\\lambda$ is the number of times it is a solution of the characteristic equation. \n\nFor example, consider a $6\\times 6$ matrix $A$ with the following characteristic equation:\n\n$$\n(\\lambda-{\\color{red}4})(\\lambda-{\\color{red}4})(\\lambda-1)(\\lambda+8)^{\\color{blue}3} =0\n$$\n\nThe eigenvalue $\\lambda={\\color{red}4}$ is a double root. Therefore, it has algebraic multiplicity $2.$ \n\nBy the same reasoning, we say that \n\n- $\\lambda=1$ has algebraic multiplicity $1,$ and\n\n- $\\lambda=-8$ has algebraic multiplicity $\\color{blue}3$." :tutorial/id #uuid "db18f185-0dce-547f-95f2-71b60a6d4d2b" :tutorial/math-academy-id 3565 :tutorial/title "The Algebraic Multiplicity of an Eigenvalue"} :step/id #uuid "37883812-d28d-5bd5-97af-2df4b9f73f66" :step/math-academy-id 20095 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186125488}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186125409 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124523 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124332 :question/id #uuid "76c52a74-9b98-5df5-ac63-64e92af1a580" :question/math-academy-id "e-5487"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5abea3ab-76a7-5598-8ede-b4cf88dd47d7" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050429} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186051061}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186125013} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186125016} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272116} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186323910} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186323911} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186366013} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186366518} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186404128} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186404378}] :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Eigenvalues of a General 3x3 Matrix"} :step/id #uuid "d8240de1-8637-5d84-886a-269d69011445" :step/math-academy-id 20096} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186125488 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124571 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124380 :question/id #uuid "a1c51187-c0a6-505c-bc58-2319b439086e" :question/math-academy-id "e-7047"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ef311af0-0e95-5574-a151-2971ad66bd08" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048505} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048669}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186125011} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186125062} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272092} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272102} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186323856} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186354507} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186366006} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186366365} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186366511}] :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Eigenvalues of a 4x4 Matrix Containing a Block of Zeros"} :step/id #uuid "1c9b6469-fe8d-5b75-bb95-efbf2684e9ce" :step/math-academy-id 25951 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186125409}}] :activity/title "The Characteristic Equation of a Matrix" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :activity.type/lesson} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186124749}]}
